<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>KhaozEngine.Gpu.D3D11</PackageId>
    <!-- Shared engine version line: <KhaozEngineVersion> in Directory.Build.props. -->
    <Version>$(KhaozEngineVersion)</Version>
    <!-- The framework is net10.0, NOT net10.0-windows, and that is decision P1 rather than an oversight. A
         windows-only TFM would stop this assembly compiling on the Linux ci.yml leg and the macOS Metal leg, and
         would stop KhaozEngine.Render.Tests referencing it unconditionally, which is where its device-free tests
         live. The Windows boundary is carried instead by [SupportedOSPlatformGuard("windows")] guards over
         [MethodImpl(MethodImplOptions.NoInlining)] [SupportedOSPlatform("windows")] bodies, the pattern
         KhaozEngine.Gpu's own D3D11ThreadingProbe already proves keeps the Vortice assembly off the load path on
         macOS and Linux. With warnings as errors, CA1416 turns that boundary into a compiler-enforced rule rather
         than a convention. -->
    <!-- ONE unsafe block in the whole package: the constant-buffer ring's copy into its mapped segment
         (D3D11UniformRing.CopyInto). A write into memory the driver handed back as a raw pointer is a raw-pointer
         write, and the alternatives are worse rather than safer: a byte[] round trip allocates per write on the
         hottest path the backend has, and the ref-arithmetic spelling of the same thing is unsafe in fact while
         reading as though it is not. Same flag KhaozEngine.Gpu, Render2D and Render3D already carry. -->
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <Description>Engine-owned native Direct3D 11 backend for the KhaozEngine.Gpu seam, and the DEFAULT backend on Windows since 17.40.0 (carried by the KhaozEngine.Game2D and KhaozEngine.Game3D umbrellas since 18.0.0, along with its two siblings, because KhaozEngine.Gpu builds no device of its own any more). Registers an IGpuBackendProvider for GpuBackendKind.Direct3D11Native through the one public entry point KhaozEngineD3D11.Register(), so a consumer outside those umbrellas opts in with a package reference plus one line at startup rather than a module initializer the CLR may never run. Targets net10.0 (not net10.0-windows) with [SupportedOSPlatformGuard("windows")] entry points over NoInlining Vortice bodies, so the assembly compiles and its device-free tests run on Linux and macOS while the Vortice.Direct3D11 interop stays off the load path there. The machine-capability probe checks the two hard device requirements the backend cannot work without, ConstantBufferOffsetting and MapNoOverwriteOnDynamicConstantBuffer. Carries no Veldrid edge of its own: the SPIRV-Cross shader path stays behind an internal, Veldrid-free cross-compile helper in KhaozEngine.Gpu.</Description>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../KhaozEngine.Gpu/KhaozEngine.Gpu.csproj" />
    <!-- The support probe says WHY a machine cannot run this backend rather than answering a bare false. Same
         dependency-free leaf the GPU seam itself carries for its backend-selection line. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="../KhaozEngine.Diagnostics/KhaozEngine.Diagnostics.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The D3D11 binding. Pinned to the same Vortice 2.3.0 line KhaozEngine.Gpu declares for its driver-threading
         probe, which is in turn pinned to what Veldrid depends on, so there is ONE D3D11 binding and one
         SharpGen.Runtime in the graph. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Vortice.Direct3D11" />
    <!-- FXC. The backend calls D3DCompile itself to vs_5_0 / ps_5_0 / cs_5_0 (decision S1), which is what buys the
         disk DXBC cache, the register numbering and a CPU-only FXC leg in CI. Declared here with the package it
         belongs to, the compile call itself lands with the shader path. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Vortice.D3DCompiler" />
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="KhaozEngine.Render.Tests" />
    <!-- The constant-buffer ring's SEMANTIC tests are shared with the native Vulkan backend (its decisions V-P5
         and V-T6): one internal test-only interface and BOTH adapters live in KhaozEngine.TestSupport.Gpu, which
         already references this package, is IsPackable=false and ships nothing. This grant is the whole visibility
         cost of that decision, and it is on THIS side because "share the tests" with no adapter on the other side
         quietly becomes one backend's tests. -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="KhaozEngine.TestSupport.Gpu" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
